# Git commits

When creating or amending commits in this repo (including research and docs):

- Use **Conventional Commits** matching `git log`: `type(scope): subject`
- Common types here: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `build`, `test`
- Prefer a **scope** when one is clear (`prepare-signing`, `theme`, `adr`, `research`)
- Subject: imperative, concise; optional body for why — not a second title
- Research write-ups use `docs(research): …`
- ADRs use `docs(adr): …`
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent@cursor.com` (or any Cursor attribution trailer). If tooling injects it, strip it before finishing the commit.

```text
# ❌ BAD
Document prepare and createSigning seams for issue #2.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
docs(research): inventory prepare and createSigning seams

# ✅ GOOD
feat(prepare-toolbar): add arrow left icon to back button
```
